    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:49b18e3fb3f9ec7b",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "71a86f15cf5c5f8aad1a2b89ac67330f822af946f3f8542bb626833720d9f03d",
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a sightseeing tour of Santiago with an English-speaking guide.\n\nThe first stop is the square by La Moneda, Chile’s government palace. The neoclassical building was built in 1799, in the final years of Spanish rule, as the royal mint. It has been the seat of Chile’s government since the mid-19th century.\n\nContinue to Plaza de Armas, the central square where Santiago’s history began. Around it stand the former governors’ residence, City Hall, the Central Post Office, the Royal Court building and the cathedral.\n\nThen head up Santa Lucía Hill for a panoramic view of the city. From the historic centre, the tour continues through the modern districts of Vitacura, Las Condes and Providencia, following the Mapocho River and the main avenues. In a single day, you can see the city’s historic administrative centre and its newer residential and business districts.\n\nAfter the city tour, visit wineries in the Maipo Valley for a tasting. Once you leave central Santiago, the dense streets give way to vineyards and the focus shifts to local wine.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-mw6kz1rj-kl1fzhzh8j"
      }
    },
